@@section 2
@@title SQ-RP Spice of Life: Raspberry Pie Addition, 2026-11-12 ([raspberry_pie.md](../raspberry_pie.md) section 14, TODO `food/types-and-tuning #21`)
@@date 2026-11-12
@@jars creativebrewing creativedelight solraspberrypie
@@sources feature_writeup/raspberry_pie.md
@@text
@@text Targets `solRaspberryPie-1.0.0.jar` of 2026-11-12 20:47 (installed in `mods/`) with Apple Pie 2.2.0, the edited
@@text `defaultconfigs/solapplepie-server.toml` (benefits empty, `resetOnDeath = false`, drink blacklist) and
@@text `defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`. Use a **fresh world** (both configs only reach new worlds). Rows marked
@@text "rebuild" also need Common + Creative Delight rebuilt (Diet Log name, Apple Pie potato recipe removed) or Creative
@@text Brewing rebuilt (Lava Walker burn); those two jars carry other unbuilt commits, so the owner rebuilds them. Most rows
@@text need a real player eating, so they are client rows (group `client`, a fresh superflat survival world, `/gamemode
@@text survival`; feed with `/give @s <food>`). Ladder thresholds below are the pack ladder's (slots at 2, 10, 30, 50, 75;
@@text flat Speed I at 20; 1 heart at 5, 15, ...); scale a check to what the world's diversity reaches.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-RPI-01 | boot: ladder loaded, no mixin errors, no Apple Pie warnings
@group A
@commands Boot. `grep -nE "solraspberrypie\|Raspberry Pie\|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie\|InvalidInjectionException" logs/latest.log` (RPI-01)
@pass `Diet ladder: N rungs, 5 slots, M pool effects` with N, M about 81, 37 (raspberry_pie.md 3.3; fewer only with one `skipped N entries` warning naming a missing mod); no mixin or injection error; no `Apple Pie's own benefit list is not empty` note; no `resetOnDeath is true` problem and no `APPLE PIE SETTINGS RASPBERRY PIE CANNOT WORK WITH` block
@fails mixin target names in `development/solRaspberryPie/.../mixin/` (Apple Pie `initPages`, `m_7856_`, `updateFoodList`, `addFood`); world copied an old `serverconfig/solapplepie-server.toml` (fresh world needed)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb passed
# r1123rp BF-FIX 2026-11-23: the pack ladder grew (raspberry_pie.md 3.3: about 81 rungs, 5 slots, 37 pool effects) and the
# Apple Pie settings lines were reworded (plan_rp_standalone.md P5, ApplePieSettings): counts read as a look
bootexpect Diet ladder: [0-9]+ rungs, 5 slots, [0-9]+ pool effects
bootreject InvalidInjectionException|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie.*failed|MixinApplyError
bootreject Apple Pie's own benefit list is not empty
bootreject resetOnDeath is true
bootreject APPLE PIE SETTINGS RASPBERRY PIE CANNOT WORK WITH
shell grep -nE "solraspberrypie|Raspberry Pie" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-300 | head -40
look the `Diet ladder:` line's rung and pool counts are about 81 and 37; any `skipped N entries` line names only ids of mods not in the pack

## SQ-RPI-02 | ladder.json seeded from defaultconfigs
@group A
@commands Same boot: `ls saves/<world>/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`; `diff` it with `defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json`
@pass file exists, identical (seeded from defaultconfigs)
@fails `LadderLoader.load` seeding path (`FMLPaths.GAMEDIR/defaultconfigs`)
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1112/rp1.qb passed
bootexpect Seeded .*ladder\.json from .*defaultconfigs
shell L=$(sed -n 's/^level-name=//p' server.properties); ls -l "$L"/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json && diff "$L"/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json defaultconfigs/solraspberrypie/ladder.json && echo IDENTICAL

## SQ-RPI-03 | unregistered and unsafe entries skipped, ladder still 38 rungs
@group A
@commands Stop. In the world's `ladder.json` add `{"threshold": 3, "type": "unlock", "effect": "nosuchmod:thing"}` and `{"threshold": 4, "type": "flat", "effect": "minecraft:absorption"}`; boot (RPI-20, RPI-35, V10)
@pass exactly one line `skipped N entries naming effects or attributes that are not registered: ...` that names `unlock nosuchmod:thing at 3.0`; one `V10: flat minecraft:absorption at 4.0 ...` warning; the `Diet ladder:` rung count equals the unedited boot's
@fails `LadderLoader.parse` skipped / warnings lists
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1112/rp2.qb
# r1123rp 2026-11-23: the edit and restart are in the row (r1120nv lost the batch prep); counts relative to the pack ladder
edit L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); F="$L/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json"; cp "$F" "$F.orig" && python3 -c 'import json,sys; f=sys.argv[1]; d=json.load(open(f)); d["rungs"]+=[{"threshold": 3, "type": "unlock", "effect": "nosuchmod:thing"}, {"threshold": 4, "type": "flat", "effect": "minecraft:absorption"}]; json.dump(d, open(f, "w"), indent=1)' "$F" && echo EDITED
restart
bootexpect skipped [0-9]+ entries naming effects or attributes that are not registered: .*unlock nosuchmod:thing at 3\.0
bootexpect V10: flat minecraft:absorption at 4\.0
bootexpect Diet ladder: [0-9]+ rungs, 5 slots
shell grep -cE "skipped [0-9]+ entries" logs/latest.log; grep -cE "V10: flat minecraft:absorption" logs/latest.log; grep -E "Diet ladder: " logs/latest.log | cut -c1-200; grep -E "Diet ladder: " logs/qrun_boot1.log | cut -c1-200; true
look exactly one skipped line and one absorption V10 line (counts above both 1); the rung count equals boot 1's (qrun_boot1.log line above): the two added rungs are both dropped

## SQ-RPI-04 | broken ladder file: loud error, built-in ladder, server runs
@group A
@commands Stop. Break the world's `ladder.json` (delete a comma); boot (V13, Q-H)
@pass `DIET LADDER FILE IS BROKEN OR MISSING` block; `Diet ladder` line absent but the server runs on the built-in ladder (`/solrp pause list` works)
@fails `LadderLoader.load` catch path; `default_ladder.json` in the jar
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@from batches/r1112/rp3.qb passed
# r1123rp 2026-11-23: edit and restart in the row; SQ-RPI-08 restores ladder.json.orig (saved by SQ-RPI-03). BF-FIX r1123rp:
# the first comma sits inside the _comment string (still valid JSON), so the file is cut in half instead
edit L=$(sed -n "s/^level-name=//p" server.properties); F="$L/serverconfig/solraspberrypie/ladder.json"; test -f "$F.orig" || cp "$F" "$F.orig"; python3 -c 'import sys; f=sys.argv[1]; t=open(f).read(); open(f, "w").write(t[:len(t) // 2])' "$F" && echo BROKEN
restart
bootexpect DIET LADDER FILE IS BROKEN OR MISSING
bootreject Diet ladder: [0-9]+ rungs, 5 slots
> solrp pause list
expect rpb|paused

